<div
  class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,24rem)] lg:items-start lg:gap-16"
  id="home-page"
>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-8">
    <p class="text-label-md uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">
      Real-time community chat
    </p>

    <h1 class="max-w-2xl text-balance text-display-lg tracking-tight text-base-content">
      Rooms, wallet, and live radio — one platform, in real time.
    </h1>

    <p class="max-w-xl text-body-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">
      BeamChat organizes conversation into rooms grouped under an admin-managed
      category tree, funds paid rooms from a per-user wallet (M-Pesa or card),
      and streams face-to-face video and live radio over LiveKit — all on one
      deployment with one set of admins.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
      <a href={~p"/auth/register"} class="btn btn-primary px-8">Create an account</a>
      <a href={~p"/auth/login"} class="btn btn-outline">Sign in</a>
    </div>

    <dl class="grid max-w-2xl grid-cols-2 gap-6 border-t border-base-300 pt-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div>
        <dt class="text-label-sm uppercase tracking-wide text-base-content/40">Transport</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold">WebSockets</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt class="text-label-sm uppercase tracking-wide text-base-content/40">Stack</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold">Elixir · LiveView</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="col-span-2 sm:col-span-1">
        <dt class="text-label-sm uppercase tracking-wide text-base-content/40">Media</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold">LiveKit</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <aside class="card bg-white border border-base-300 shadow-panel rounded-box p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-headline-sm">What's inside</h2>

    <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-4 text-sm text-base-content/70">
      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-xs font-bold text-primary">
          <.icon name="hero-check" class="size-3.5" />
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Rooms with a structure.</strong>
          Public, private, secret, and paid rooms hanging off a category
          tree of arbitrary depth.
        </span>
      </li>

      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-xs font-bold text-primary">
          <.icon name="hero-banknotes" class="size-3.5" />
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">A wallet that pays for rooms.</strong>
          Top up with M-Pesa (STK push) or card; a paid room is unlocked by a
          time-boxed subscription, debited atomically.
        </span>
      </li>

      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-xs font-bold text-primary">
          <.icon name="hero-shield-check" class="size-3.5" />
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Moderation with a paper trail.</strong>
          Word, link, and pattern rules run before persistence — every block
          and flag is logged.
        </span>
      </li>

      <li class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="flex size-6 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-xs font-bold text-primary">
          <.icon name="hero-signal" class="size-3.5" />
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong class="font-semibold text-base-content">Video and radio over LiveKit.</strong>
          In-room face-to-face calls and admin-run radio stations, published
          straight into LiveKit rooms.
        </span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="mt-6 rounded-md border border-base-200 bg-base-100 p-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">
      One deployment, one set of admins: roles, bans, payment providers,
      and the category structure are managed from a single settings surface.
      API health check: <a href="/health" class="link font-medium link-primary">GET /health</a>
    </div>
  </aside>
</div>
